            <ArticleTitle>[Lumboradiculalgia and calcified disk hernia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>763-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the context of a particular case report, the authors recall that calcified discs may be responsible for root pain, hyperalgic sciatica or lumbago. In the present case, the pain responded to intra-discal injection of long-acting corticosteroids. The authors compare this case to 10 other personal cases and 16 cases reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
